also a lot of festering feces in that same pile that is the Star Wars EU, and I will not be the least bit sorry to see it go. As Blue Fox stated, there is 30 years of the stuff to go through. That is a lot of work to determine what is good and what is BS. I strongly suspected if anything of the EU survives, it'll be a &quot;in the broadstrokes only&quot; kind of deal, and will most likely be completely redone anyway in a matter that fits with Disney's new direction for the franchise. Does this mean some gems are likely to be lost in that process? Probably, but it also means that we don't have to try and reconcile some things that were rendered as continuity snarls by the prequel trilogy and other acts of Lucas (and soon to be acts of Disney). So, for now anyway, I'm interested to see what they do, and am fully prepped to accept that the old EU is gone. Of course, I'm prepped to go the other way (not that it will do any good), if the new Star Wars universe is not up to my standards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: Unless stated otherwise, all examples I give are completely random and almost assuredly pulled from my nethers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1575-dairugger","name":"Dairugger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1575_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T06:34:29-08:00","id":45543,"title":"","content":"I have the uncomfortable thought that many just elected Disney &quot;Supreme Chancellor&quot; with applause, cheers, and fanfare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","u