":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T19:28:49-08:00","id":46000,"title":"","content":"I think it might be good to have an outlet for that stuff anyway. Just in case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T05:55:42-08:00","id":46193,"title":"","content":"Yea, hard to say who owns the rights to what. I'd assume that Lucasfilm owed all the rights for the characters and stories while Dark Horse had the rights to publish it all. But, Lucasfilm is now Disney, so who knows.<br /> <br /> Sounds like a huge legal mess to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T06:20:42-08:00","id":46207,"title":"","content":"If its as you think it is, then Disney has the writes to publish that material again if they want to. If all Dark Horse had a license to create (with Lucasfilm permission), publish and distribute comics involving Star Wars, the legal matter is rather simple. With the license gone they no longer have a say in what happens to those stories at all, and Disney could pile it on to one big bonfire and claim the stuff never existed with Dark Horse not being able to do anything official about it. However, it can become a legal mess if Dark Horse actually owned any part of it. If they own parts of the stories they did for Star Wars, and Disney wants to use them (the other half of the legal nightmare question) then there is a mess. If Disney opts not to use any of it, then all they need do is identify what part of the previous mythos is owned by Dark Horse and put a big stamp on it saying &quot;DO NOT USE, EVER!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: Unless stated otherwise, all examples I give are completely random and almost assuredly pulled from my nethers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1575-dairugger","name":"Dairugger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1575_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T06:30:19-08:00","id":46210,"title":"","content":"All Dark Horse has to do is throw it all on the 'net for free and say it's fan-made material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T07:04:09-08:00","id":46229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dairugger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/41828-star-wars-comics-move-to-marvel-in-2015?p=46207#post46207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If its as you think it is, then Disney has the writes to publish that material again if they want to. If all Dark Horse had a license to create (with Lucasfilm permission), publish and distribute comics involving Star Wars, the legal matter is rather simple. With the license gone they no longer have a say in what happens to those stories at all, and Disney could pile it on to one big bonfire and claim the stuff never existed with Dark Horse not being able to do anything official about it. However, it can become a legal mess if Dark Horse actually owned any part of it. If they own parts of the stories they did for Star Wars, and Disney wants to use them (the other half of the legal nightmare question) then there is a mess. If Disney opts not to use any of it, then all they need do is identify what part of the previous mythos is owned by Dark Horse and put a big stamp on it saying &quot;DO NOT USE, EVER!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yea, without more detail it's hard to say. I'll be curious to hear who retains the rights to what. In a case like this, I'm just not sure who has what rights.<br /> <br /> Maybe if Lucasfilm/Disney decides to keep the Dark Horse continunity canon, then Dark Horse might have rights to reprint their comics though they might not be making new ones, while Marvel will pick up where left off?<br /> <br /> I have no idea what they're gonna do. I'm glad I'm not included in trying to sort out the legality of all that...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T21:16:53-08:00","id":46736,"title":"","content":"No issues really. I am 100% sure the office who kept track of Star Wars continuity transferred what they had over to Disney, and these legal issues were hammered out with Dark Horse long before they wrote their first line of dialogue or drew the first Jedi. As Disney bought Lucasfilm, all the contracts transfer accordingly. If anything, there is someone whose job is to make sure everyone follows the rules, as opposed to figuring out what the rules should be in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T17:55:12-08:00","id":49391,"title":"","content":"As if to answer our question, Disney has formed the Lucasfilm Story Group. Leland Chee, a member of the group, spoke about canon this week. They are eliminating all the layers of canon, and doing away with the EU. Some small parts of the EU will be folded into canon, and then forevermore there will be 'canon' and 'not canon.' The EU is dead, and they are tossing most of it out.<br /> <br /> Now the question is, what gems will make the final cut? It is too early to know for sure, so we just have to wait for the LSG to tell us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T18:13:28-08:00","id":49409,"title":"","content":"I wish Timothy Zahn's original trilogy of books would make the cut, but the prequels already invalidated it, so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T19:01:16-08:00","id":49453,"title":"","content":"They ALL make the cut..Some just won't be &quot;Disney.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T21:52:48-08:00","id":49558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/41828-star-wars-comics-move-to-marvel-in-2015?p=49409#post49409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish Timothy Zahn's original trilogy of books would make the cut, but the prequels already invalidated it, so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I was thinking the same thing. Zahn's books will always be my favorite part of the EU, and I will always have beef with Lucas for messing with them. I don't think he sees it that way, but the hints of the Clone Wars we saw in Zahn's trilogy were far better than what Lucas gave us in the prequel films.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T07:12:23-08:00","id":49760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/41828-star-wars-comics-move-to-marvel-in-2015?p=49409#post49409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish Timothy Zahn's original trilogy of books would make the cut, but the prequels already invalidated it, so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still wish they had made those into movies. But it waaaay too late for that.<br /> <br /> But yea, Lucas screwed us all with the prequels and how it contradicted alot of the EU. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Of course, if you ignore the Prequels like I'm pretty much doing, then it's all good. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/41828-star-wars-comics-move-to-marvel-in-2015?p=49558#post49558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I was thinking the same thing. Zahn's books will always be my favorite part of the EU, and I will always have beef with Lucas for messing with them. I don't think he sees it that way, but the hints of the Clone Wars we saw in Zahn's trilogy were far better than what Lucas gave us in the prequel films.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree. The way clones were used in those books were a hell of alot better than what we got in the Prequels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T08:06:22-08:00","id":49800,"title":"","content":"Heres another article about it. <a href=\"http://arstechnica.com/gadgets/2014/01/op-ed-disney-takes-a-chainsaw-to-the-star-wars-expanded-universe/\" target=\"_blank\">http://arstechnica.com/gadgets/2014/...nded-universe/</a><br /> <br /> That one makes it sound like most, if not all the EU stuff is going bye bye and a new single &quot;official&quot; canon will be constructed. Not sure how ture that is, so take it with a grain of salt...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T10:08:39-08:00","id":49878,"title":"","content":"As I said before, I'm inclined to believe that the old EU is going away. If anything persists, it'll be a small handful of really cool gem (which will promptly be reshaped) and possibly a handful of nods to the old EU but something on the scale of &quot;blink and you miss it&quot; styled cameos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: Unless stated otherwise, all examples I give are completely random and almost assuredly pulled from my nethers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1575-dairugger","name":"Dairugger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1575_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T10:12:53-08:00","id":49880,"title":"","content":"Heres another good article on the subject: <a href=\"http://observationdeck.io9.com/what-does-the-new-disney-star-wars-canon-policy-mean-to-1500616623\" target=\"_blank\">http://observationdeck.io9.com/what-...-to-1500616623</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T10:13:49-08:00","id":49882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dairugger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/41828-star-wars-comics-move-to-marvel-in-2015?p=49878#post49878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said before, I'm inclined to believe that the old EU is going away. If anything persists, it'll be a small handful of really cool gem (which will promptly be reshaped) and possibly a handful of nods to the old EU but something on the scale of &quot;blink and you miss it&quot; styled cameos.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yup, thats what I'd think as well...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T11:05:44-08:00","id":49926,"title":"","content":"I'm actually thinking they'll end up declaring a blank slate and only importing the EU elements as they need/want/can-sell them. Really if you're declaring everything non-canon until you say otherwise, what's the hurry to make anything canon? Particularly when you can sell Hurry-Up-And-Make-This-Canon-Or-Not to game developers and book writers as a service.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T11:33:10-08:00","id":49943,"title":"","content":"True. At this point, they might as well wipe the slate clean. But will do that for all EU material, or just post ROTJ material? There was tons of Lucasfilm approved prequel era novels and such, and of course theres tons of Old Republic stuff. Of course, I guess it was all Lucasfilm approved stuff at some point in time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T11:49:17-08:00","id":49950,"title":"","content":"Why keep any of it? Almost all of it seems rather ad-hoc. If continuity happened at all, it was because the writers cared about it and had read it. Other than that, it was mostly people making things up as they went and just trying to make it sound Star Wars-y. The better idea for Disney is to define at least high level canon and fill out details as they currently have plans. This would allow them to develop a very consistent feel to the universe. By high-level canon, I mean very clearly define what the Force can and, more importantly, cannot do, or to define what the effect of a blaster by size is, crap like that. Granted a lot of that basic ground work is done, by there is also quite a lot about what the tech and Force of Star Wars can and cannot do that was defined by the EU, and it makes sense to at least make a document that clearly states: You can't use the Force to resurrect the dead, but you can use Force Lightning without utilizing the Dark Side, if you do it through enlightened use of the Force rather than rage-induced brute forcing it (hence why dark siders seem to use it so often, they are using a short cut that may come back to bite them in the end, whereas a non-darksider may need centuries of meditating on the Force before they realize it is even possible for them to use it).<br /> <br /> By the way, any examples I give are 100%, completely random and pulled from my nether regions, do not nit pick any of them as they aren't meant to stand up to scrutiny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: Unless stated otherwise, all examples I give are completely random and almost assuredly pulled from my nethers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1575-dairugger","name":"Dairugger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1575_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T16:30:55-08:00","id":50220,"title":"","content":"I am not part of the LSG, but if I was, my first topic of business would be cutting Midi-chlorians... and any movie mentioning them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T17:14:54-08:00","id":50257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/41828-star-wars-comics-move-to-marvel-in-2015?p=50220#post50220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not part of the LSG, but if I was, my first topic of business would be cutting Midi-chlorians... and any movie mentioning them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>My thoughts exactly! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T17:18:17-08:00","id":50261,"title":"","content":"Just to say, until the Prequels came out, most of the EU stuff stuck fairly close to the movies and was essentially all in a continuity. The prequels is really what changed alot of that...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dairugger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/41828-star-wars-comics-move-to-marvel-in-2015?p=49950#post49950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The better idea for Disney is to define at least high level canon and fill out details as they currently have plans. This would allow them to develop a very consistent feel to the universe. By high-level canon, I mean very clearly define what the Force can and, more importantly, cannot do, or to define what the effect of a blaster by size is, crap like that. Granted a lot of that basic ground work is done, by there is also quite a lot about what the tech and Force of Star Wars can and cannot do that was defined by the EU, and it makes sense to at least make a document that clearly states: You can't use the Force to resurrect the dead, but you can use Force Lightning without utilizing the Dark Side, if you do it through enlightened use of the Force rather than rage-induced brute forcing it (hence why dark siders seem to use it so often, they are using a short cut that may come back to bite them in the end, whereas a non-darksider may need centuries of meditating on the Force before they realize it is even possible for them to use it).<br /> <br /> By the way, any examples I give are 100%, completely random and pulled from my nether regions, do not nit pick any of them as they aren't meant to stand up to scrutiny.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can agree with that...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T17:27:15-08:00","id":50275,"title":"","content":"I just really really *really* hope they decide to ret-con eliminate the force as a STD thing.<br /> <br /> And the force detection by hitting a little piece of brain.<br /> <br /> I could tolerate the force detection by uncommon and specifically focused technology though, provided it's only detection, very fussy and short-range.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T18:14:03-08:00","id":51261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/41828-star-wars-comics-move-to-marvel-in-2015?p=50275#post50275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just really really *really* hope they decide to ret-con eliminate the force as a STD thing.<br /> <br /> And the force detection by hitting a little piece of brain.<br /> <br /> I could tolerate the force detection by uncommon and specifically focused technology though, provided it's only detection, very fussy and short-range.</div> </div> </div> </div>Geek heresy time: I actually kinda like the idea behind midi-chlorians. I didn't until quite recently, but after reading about Darth Plagueis - a Sith Lord with unmatched power to manipulate midi-chlorians with the Force, and through them to manipulate life - the idea of the Force as something which exerts a biological influence over people seems awesome to me. I would, however, still like to get rid of the idea that you can measure Force sensitivity with a simple blood test.<br /> <br /> In fact, I'd rather not involve technology at all in Force detection. I'd sooner just leave that as an ability unique to Force users - no blood tests, no radar scanners, just a Jedi dude who puts hand to his temple and mutters something about sensing a resonance in the Force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T22:19:53-08:00","id":51397,"title":"","content":"\u201cSize matters not. Look at me. Judge me by my size, do you? Hmm? Hmm. And well you should not. For my ally is the Force, and a powerful ally it is. Life creates it, makes it grow. Its energy surrounds us and binds us. Luminous beings are we, not this crude matter. You must feel the Force around you; here, between you, me, the tree, the rock, everywhere, yes. Even between the land and the ship.\u201d<br /> <br /> This quote from Yoda is why I have never liked the midi-chlorians. Midis in the rocks and ship? Between them? Or midis floating in the air? Or some other explanation? Sure, there are ways to reinterpret this quote to make it work with the midis, but it feels too much like redefining the essence of the Force from one trilogy to the next. That doesn't sit well with me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T23:08:17-08:00","id":51420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cielle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/41828-star-wars-comics-move-to-marvel-in-2015?p=51261#post51261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Geek heresy time: I actually kinda like the idea behind midi-chlorians. I didn't until quite recently, but after reading about Darth Plagueis - a Sith Lord with unmatched power to manipulate midi-chlorians with the Force, and through them to manipulate life - the idea of the Force as something which exerts a biological influence over people seems awesome to me. I would, however, still like to get rid of the idea that you can measure Force sensitivity with a simple blood test.<br /> <br /> In fact, I'd rather not involve technology at all in Force detection. I'd sooner just leave that as an ability unique to Force users - no blood tests, no radar scanners, just a Jedi dude who puts hand to his temple and mutters something about sensing a resonance in the Force.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is lost if Plagueis has unmatched power to manipulate life via the Force rather through the force to symbiotic or parasitic bacteria that in turn effect the host?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T00:14:04-08:00","id":51444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/41828-star-wars-comics-move-to-marvel-in-2015?p=49880#post49880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heres another good article on the subject: <a href=\"http://observationdeck.io9.com/what-does-the-new-disney-star-wars-canon-policy-mean-to-1500616623\" target=\"_blank\">http://observationdeck.io9.com/what-...-to-1500616623</a></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Above all though, Disney actually <i>does</i> listen to the fanbase - provided the voice is loud enough. </div> </div> </div>Forgive them Father. They know not what they do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T05:45:59-08:00","id":51561,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://techland.time.com/2010/08/10/20000-per-cell-why-midi-chlorians-suck/\" target=\"_blank\">Why Midichlorians Suck</a><br /> <i> One word ruined Star Wars for me, and probably for a generation of fans, too. That word wasn\u2019t Jar Jar or Watto. It wasn\u2019t a character.<br /> It was \u201cmidi-chlorians.\u201d<br /> With that one word, the mechanisms of the Force became less spiritual and more scientific. Major bummer. The draw of the concept of the Force in the Original Trilogy is that it comes across as a low-maintenance religion. It\u2019s kinda like Unitarianism that also gives you psychic powers and enables you to jump, fight and stare better than other members of your respective species. (Seriously, Jedi wield eye contact like a weapon. Never get into a staring contest with them.) You couldn\u2019t measure the Force really, unless it whopped you upside the head. It was just there, lingering like a threat or a promise.<br /> Until, of course, \u201cmidi-chlorians.\u201d<br /> Moreover, \u201cmidi-chlorians\u201d messes up every extrapolated wish fulfillment that accompanies Star Wars, too. Every kid who ever wanted to be a Jedi thought that all they\u2019d have to do was train really hard, learn to concentrate and squint and they\u2019d somehow connect to the energy that moves through all living things. But that stupid little Force Detector Qui-Gon pulls out in Phantom Menace scuttled the hopes of all such young dreamers. Forget about all those push-ups and those eyebrow raises you\u2019ve been practicing. If you\u2019ve got a low midi-chlorian count, won\u2019t be no Jedi Academy for you, youngling.<br /> I know my lament isn\u2019t a new thing and is just another voice added to the angry nerd chorus. Maybe this is too far a tangent, but when that device gets whipped out in Episode One, the line separating Star Trek and Star Wars blurs. The former series is about the empirical investigation of the universe, with technology at the forefront. The latter is more sociological, turning on the strength of personal belief and political will to change history.<br /> \u201cMidi-chlorians\u201d take all the comparative religion ideas, all the quasi-mythological essences that churn at the core of Star Wars and turn them into easily quantifiable biology. And metaphor or not, I say \u201cboo\u201d to all that.<br /> </i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T06:22:30-08:00","id":53940,"title":"","content":"Not exactly Star Wars comics related...but...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://io9.com/is-star-wars-boba-fett-movie-going-to-be-about-a-whole-1504770166?utm_campaign=socialflow_io9_facebook&amp;utm_source=io9_facebook&amp;utm_medium=socialflow\" target=\"_blank\">http://io9.com/is-star-wars-boba-fet...ium=socialflow</a><br /> <br /> That mentions the possibility of the rumored Boba Fett movie being about a guy who kills Fett and takes his armor and name. Now that I can get behind. Apparently, if the rumor is true, Lawrence Kasdan didn't like Boba Fetts origin in the prequels.<br /> <br /> How awesome would it be if Fett in the OT isn't the same dude from the prequels? That'd be awesome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T11:00:15-08:00","id":54090,"title":"","content":"That would be an interesting twist on the story, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T13:22:39-08:00","id":54189,"title":"","content":"Huh. I either closed the tab before actually posting or the forum ate my post. Either way, let me try again =/<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/41828-star-wars-comics-move-to-marvel-in-2015?p=53940#post53940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not exactly Star Wars comics related...but...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://io9.com/is-star-wars-boba-fett-movie-going-to-be-about-a-whole-1504770166?utm_campaign=socialflow_io9_facebook&amp;utm_source=io9_facebook&amp;utm_medium=socialflow\" target=\"_blank\">http://io9.com/is-star-wars-boba-fet...ium=socialflow</a><br /> <br /> That mentions the possibility of the rumored Boba Fett movie being about a guy who kills Fett and takes his armor and name. Now that I can get behind. Apparently, if the rumor is true, Lawrence Kasdan didn't like Boba Fetts origin in the prequels.<br /> <br /> How awesome would it be if Fett in the OT isn't the same dude from the prequels? That'd be awesome!</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall there was some tradition in the old days of the Mandalorians for all their top leader to adopt the name Mandalore. I also seen to remember at least one instance in which a dude earned the title after retrieving the helmet of a former Mandalore. And taking leadership by a combat challenge is well within their culture too. So it would make some sense that Boba Fett, considered &quot;last of the Mandalorians&quot; could also be a name &quot;inherited&quot; by force.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T13:43:45-08:00","id":54208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/41828-star-wars-comics-move-to-marvel-in-2015?p=54090#post54090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be an interesting twist on the story, yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd love it!! I was not a fan of them including Boba Fett in the prequels, so this would be amazing to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/41828-star-wars-comics-move-to-marvel-in-2015?p=54189#post54189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall there was some tradition in the old days of the Mandalorians for all their top leader to adopt the name Mandalore. I also seen to remember at least one instance in which a dude earned the title after retrieving the helmet of a former Mandalore. And taking leadership by a combat challenge is well within their culture too. So it would make some sense that Boba Fett, considered &quot;last of the Mandalorians&quot; could also be a name &quot;inherited&quot; by force.</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw you mention that in the other thread. Looks like they really expanded on them since I was last into the EU, Clone Wars aside where the culture is alive and well apparently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a hr